blican-favorable columns, most calling it Solid or Safe Republican, and prediction markets give Democrats about a one-in-seven chance.\n\nDemocrat Nicole Locklin, a first-time challenger, has raised about $348,000 and drawn local coverage and an endorsement from a group backing Democrats in flippable seats, but no public polls have tested the matchup. The national political environment this year leans Democratic, which keeps the seat from being entirely out of reach on paper. Still, the combination of incumbency, money, and district partisanship points to a Republican hold of roughly ten points.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0585, "margin": -10.04}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0347, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0316, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0629, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0423, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0476, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0418, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.063, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0712, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0314, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0905, "margin": -10.0}]}